  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 115 AM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nThursday through Tuesday:\n\nHigh pressure returns on Thursday, with cloud cover slowly\nexiting as low pressure continues to weaken to the southeast.\nExpecting highs in the upper 70s to low 80s, with light and\nvariable winds. High pressure lingers through the overnight\nhours, bringing lows in the upper 50s to low 60s. \n\nFriday, winds will shift to southerly as high pressure\npropagates eastward and low pressure propagates into the Hudson\nBay. Expect increasing temperatures and humidity, with highs in\nthe low 80s. Saturday, southerly winds continue, with highs in\nthe mid-80s. Isolated pop-up storms are possible as a weak\nsurface front moves through northern Wisconsin (~15% chances). \n\nSaturday night into Sunday, low pressure in the northern Plains\nwill begin to bring frontogenesis/upper level ridging to the \nwestern Great Lakes region, and a return to an active weather \npattern through early next week. Expect increasing heat and \nhumidity, with highs in the mid to upper 80s and heat index \nvalues around 90 degrees. Multiple shortwaves riding over the \nupper level ridging will serve as the basis for rain and storm \nchances Sunday through Tuesday, with exact timing and therefore\nintensity remaining uncertain at this time (30-50% PoPs\nthroughout the time period will be refined as individual\nshortwaves become more clear later this week).\n\nMH",
